WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.200
Mangroves: four things people

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.140
say about them, and what the

3
00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.850
sources say back.

4
00:00:07.416 --> 00:00:10.076
People say a mangrove forest is

5
00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:12.946
just a muddy wasteland. Myth.

6
00:00:13.503 --> 00:00:14.883
The fact:

7
00:00:14.883 --> 00:00:16.943
mangroves help hold the coast

8
00:00:16.943 --> 00:00:20.263
against erosion, store carbon

9
00:00:20.263 --> 00:00:22.003
and support fisheries.

10
00:00:22.003 --> 00:00:24.263
A scheme called MISHTI plants

11
00:00:24.263 --> 00:00:25.173
more.

12
00:00:25.603 --> 00:00:28.143
Others say no tree can live with

13
00:00:28.143 --> 00:00:31.593
its feet in salt water. Myth.

14
00:00:32.059 --> 00:00:33.399
The fact:

15
00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:35.299
mangroves grow where tides

16
00:00:35.299 --> 00:00:38.119
reach, roots under water.

17
00:00:38.119 --> 00:00:40.779
In airless mud, some roots

18
00:00:40.779 --> 00:00:43.319
simply grow upward to breathe.

19
00:00:43.319 --> 00:00:45.509
A sensible arrangement.

20
00:00:46.114 --> 00:00:47.914
Then there is the claim that the

21
00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:50.134
Sundarbans are India's only

22
00:00:50.134 --> 00:00:52.244
mangroves. Myth.

23
00:00:52.641 --> 00:00:53.781
The fact:

24
00:00:53.781 --> 00:00:56.361
mangroves also line the deltas

25
00:00:56.361 --> 00:00:58.761
of the Mahanadi, Krishna,

26
00:00:58.761 --> 00:01:01.061
Godavari and Kaveri.

27
00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:03.521
West Bengal, home of the

28
00:01:03.521 --> 00:01:05.561
Sundarbans, holds the largest

29
00:01:05.561 --> 00:01:06.491
share.

30
00:01:06.941 --> 00:01:08.161
And last:

31
00:01:08.161 --> 00:01:11.001
tigers keep to dry forests.

32
00:01:11.001 --> 00:01:12.031
Myth.

33
00:01:12.442 --> 00:01:13.282
The fact:

34
00:01:13.282 --> 00:01:15.402
the Royal Bengal Tiger is the

35
00:01:15.402 --> 00:01:16.902
famous resident of these

36
00:01:16.902 --> 00:01:19.562
mangrove forests, with turtles,

37
00:01:19.562 --> 00:01:21.362
crocodiles and snakes for

38
00:01:21.362 --> 00:01:22.533
neighbours.

39
00:01:23.433 --> 00:01:24.033
For GS3:

40
00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:26.193
India's mangroves cover about

41
00:01:26.193 --> 00:01:27.606
four thousand nine hundred

42
00:01:27.606 --> 00:01:29.073
ninety two square kilometres,

43
00:01:29.073 --> 00:01:32.253
under a fifth of one percent of

44
00:01:32.253 --> 00:01:32.613
